<title>MEXICO: Mexico Minsa buys Texas corn mill from ADM.</title>
<headline>Mexico Minsa buys Texas corn mill from ADM.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican corn flour company Grupo Minsa said Tuesday it bought a 75,000-tonne-per-year corn milling plant from ADM Milling Corp, a unit of Archer Daniels Midland Inc.</p>
<p>Minsa gave no details of the amount of the transaction paid for the mill in Muleshoe, Texas, but added the purchase included 56 hectares of adjacent land and the mill's client portfolio.</p>
<p>&quot;We are also contemplating the option to buy a grains warehousing complex of 60,000 tonnes capacity (which is alongside the mill),&quot; Minsa said in a statement.</p>
</text>
